/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  flowsheetDict  --  inletState01_undeclared_vapour

  THE STATE A UNIT COMPUTES WITH MUST BE THE STATE ITS INLET MEANS.

    feedA (450 K, 3 bar) --> [V1 valve: 1.5 bar] --> throttled --+
                                                                 +--> [M1 mixer] --> mixed
    feedB (420 K, 1.5 bar) --------------------------------------+

    feedC (420 K, 1.5 bar) --> [S1 splitter: 0.3 / 0.7] --> sideA + sideB

  The three feeds are benzene/toluene, each well above its dew point at its
  own pressure, and NONE declares `phase`.  A stream file that declares no
  phase does not thereby declare a liquid: its (T, P, z) means its own
  equilibrium, and here that equilibrium is all vapour.  The stream record
  still carries a default `vf = 0` until something resolves it, and for a
  domain inlet nothing upstream does -- so each unit that reads its inlet's
  phase resolves it itself, at the inlet's own (T, P, z), in its own thermo
  world (`flashState::resolvedInletVaporFraction`, the one home):

    * V1 (valve).  The isenthalpic let-down prices H_in on the inlet's phase.
      Read as a liquid, H_in is a liquid's and the outlet search lands tens
      of kelvin colder, part-condensed -- a valve that "condenses" a vapour.
      Read as what it is, an ideal-gas vapour has no Joule-Thomson effect
      and T_out = T_in.
    * M1 (mixer).  The inlets' phases price the inlet enthalpies AND vote for
      the outlet's dominant phase.  feedB is the LARGER inlet (150 against
      100 kmol/h) on purpose: the valve's outlet is a PRODUCED vapour that
      votes vapour either way, so only an authored inlet that carries the
      vote can show a mixer reading it as a liquid -- its vapour would then
      leave labelled a liquid.
    * S1 (splitter).  A splitter preserves the phase -- the phase the inlet
      MEANS.  Its branches are PRODUCED streams that nobody re-resolves, so
      copying the carried default would publish two vapours as liquids.

  The plant's first law closes only if the units and the energy report read
  the same states.  check_inlet_resolution arm (i) runs this case and holds
  all three readings and the closure.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        V1;
        type        valve;
        in          feedA;
        outputs     ( throttled );

        operation   { P 1.5 bar; }
    }
    {
        name        M1;
        type        mixer;
        inputs      ( throttled  feedB );
        outputs     ( mixed );
    }
    {
        name        S1;
        type        splitter;
        in          feedC;
        outputs     ( sideA  sideB );

        operation   { fractions ( 0.3 0.7 ); }
    }
);
